<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan to issue tender to sell 1H June gas oil.</title>
<headline>Taiwan to issue tender to sell 1H June gas oil.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) is expected to issue a tender to sell 225,000-250,000 barrels of 0.3 percent sulphur gas oil for first half June lifting later Wednesday, company sources said.</p>
<p>The tender is due to close on May 13 and offers will be valid for two days. Offers are to be made on a free-on-board (fob) Kaoshiung basis.</p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC sold one cargo at around $25.20 per barrel for end April lifting fob Kaoshiung, traders said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-970 3093)</p>
</text>
